@@ -58,6 +58,9 @@ No `patches.py`. `op_mode` stays docked: Odyssey only takes its motion moves in
 
 General host and tool changes first needed here; each applies to every game:
 
+- **Storage-write tracking follow-up:** [A size-zero storage write needlessly invalidates every partial uniform shadow](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#a-size-zero-storage-write-needlessly-invalidates-every-partial-uniform-shadow). The upstream host correction is ported and tested with synthetic native bookkeeping; Odyssey GPU behavior and performance remain unmeasured.
+- **Shader build sidecars:** [AppleDouble files are not shader build outputs](../../../docs/reference/packing.md#appledouble-files-are-not-shader-build-outputs). Exact output-name filtering preserves the existing shader/cache identity.
+
 - **Raw capture byte widths:** [Raw snapshots guessed four bytes for wider pixel formats](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#raw-snapshots-guessed-four-bytes-for-wider-pixel-formats). Uses the existing format mapping; no rendering change.
 
 - **Array-layer HDR diagnostics:** [Raw snapshots read the wrong array layer](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#raw-render-target-snapshots-read-the-wrong-array-layer). Capture correctness only; this does not fix or explain gameplay bloom.
@@ -88,3 +91,14 @@ General host and tool changes first needed here; each applies to every game:
 - The silent first minute of sound.
 - development.md calls SDK 7.3.2 "the oldest so far"; Mario Kart 8 Deluxe (SDK 4.4.0) is older now.
 - `game.tsv` says values marked "Mario's" are not measured yet, but none is marked.
+
+
+## Experimental launcher display profile
+
+The `DM_ODYSSEY_DISPLAY_PROFILE=launcher` rewrite pairs original-word-checked observation gates with the host's `ODYSSEY_DISPLAY_V1` controls. It supports stock, 720p, 900p and 1080p targets plus optional vertical FOV extension to 4:3. The coordinated high-resolution rewrite also offers 1440p and native output when their packaged capabilities are present. The host reads the choice after the launcher and preloader join, verifies the exact main build and paired gates, checks the selected private graphics-quality overlay hash, then changes only the saved dimension arguments and projection S2/S3 values. The original projection setter recalculates its caches and frustum. Square and already-4:3 inputs are skipped. The iOS view and touch normalization use the accepted picture aspect.
+
+An explicit stock/off selection leaves the register frame and existing overlays unchanged. Handheld mode ignores stale display choices. The quality overlays preserve all non-dimension fields; no shader source, compiler options, cache epoch or PSO key schema changes. The full dynamic quality ladder still applies, so a target is not a per-frame resolution guarantee. Keep the original Guest and RomFS for rollback. Higher modes require the coordinated RT and global-heap gates; the global-heap callback registers before early returns and restores the original allocation when a choice is rejected.
+
+**F3 device observation, 2026-10-29:** the user reports working resolution switching and smooth native 2732x2048 gameplay on an 8 GB iPad Air M2, with high RAM use and little perceived improvement over 1080p. The 4:3 world view is reported correct; text and main-menu proportions remain distorted. Bloom/lighting flashes and short first-encounter hitches remain. These are user observations, not controlled frame-time, memory, or visual A/B measurements.
+
+**F4 default:** 1080p is recommended for memory efficiency and is the default for an unset supported display selection. Saved native, 1440p and stock values and explicit environment overrides retain precedence. When the launcher is skipped, the host adopts 1080p only for the exact docked build with complete display gates and validated assets; the standalone policy parser still treats an absent choice as stock. The 4:3 option stays off by default. A 4:3 1080p target is 1440x1080; wide 1080p is 1920x1080. No F4 device result is claimed.
