 - **Symptom:** a long-frame diagnostic's combined creation time exceeds the distinct pipeline and shader-library work it is meant to describe.
 - **Cause:** the inclusive pipeline timer includes prediction. Prediction's parallel prefetch and direct shader loads also increment the library timer, so adding both counters repeats their nested interval. The separate window summaries intentionally retain inclusive timings and must not be summed.
-- **Fix:** both predictor call sites use one accounting wrapper. It retains inclusive counters and records the nested library subset. Long-frame `in all` and TSV `@make_ms` use library plus pipeline minus nested library time. `@lib_ms`, `@pso_inclusive_ms` and `@predict_lib_ms` expose the components. Invalid deltas or overlap produce an explicit unknown value, never unsigned underflow or a fabricated zero. Rendering, prediction order and caches are unchanged.
