+
+## Shader build outputs
+
+### AppleDouble files are not shader build outputs
+
+- **Symptom:** a build on exFAT or FAT finishes its Metal libraries, then `c1_guard.py` stops with a UTF-8 decoding error; Metal cache prefill may reject an otherwise valid folder.
+- **Cause:** macOS writes binary `._<name>` sidecars. Suffix-only enumeration treated those files as shaders or reflection records.
+- **Fix:** table generation and Metal prefill accept only the shader builder's hexadecimal-key output names. This ports [upstream 9791d74](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/9791d74c67f4811f839331b2dbcfa906a3a9291c), retaining this fork's Windows copy handling. The tools are outside the translation-chain identity; no runtime shader semantics, library identity or existing cache files change.
+- **Check:** synthetic invalid UTF-8 sidecars are ignored while the real shader still enters its table, and compatible libraries still prefill. No game rebuild is needed to test the enumeration.
+- **Found on:** upstream PR #555; audited during the [Odyssey iPad follow-up](../../dm/games/0100000000010000/README.md#found-on-this-game). This is build-tool robustness, not a bloom or gameplay-stutter fix.
