+### A size-zero storage write needlessly invalidates every partial uniform shadow
+
+- **Symptom:** writable storage bindings of size zero set the submission-wide unknown-write flag, refusing partial uniform shadows even in a different pool and ending their render passes.
+- **Cause:** the write tracker treated a known Metal buffer with unspecified binding size as a write anywhere, and kept large writes only through a bounded page set.
+- **Fix:** port [upstream f293a70](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/f293a70fd6c2fc820473a7e30767fdf49b8e6e7c): track the remaining bytes of the resolved buffer, retain large writes as bounded intervals, and forward those intervals with the submission fence. Merge all overlapping intervals; overflow, unknown sizes and exhausted capacity keep the conservative global fallback. Shader libraries, PSO keys and cache identities are unchanged.
